     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Helvetica\">HI ggplot2 Developpers</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Helvetica;min-height:14px\"><br></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Helvetica\">Many thanks for all the hard work you put into this development.</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Helvetica;min-height:14px\"><br></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Helvetica\">I am reporting an inconsistency or bug I came across.</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;font-size:14px;line-height:normal;font-family:Helvetica\">I thought the code should pick up that a discrete scale is required for color even though the variable is not a factor. Mostly it does.</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Helvetica;min-height:14px\"><br></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Helvetica\">Here is an example. I am creating a scatterplot with a linear regression line using Deducer as GUI.</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Helvetica\">I want to construct two regression lines grouped by Colour.</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Helvetica\">This works well if the group for instance Treatment is a factor to start with.</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Helvetica\">If I use Treatment as a double, smooths correctly assigns “as.factor(Treatment)”, but not so point where “Treatment” is added only and, as a consequence, plotting is hanging. Point by itself does work though.</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Helvetica\">I have attached 3 screenshots  displaying the issue and the working setrings, and a detailed seesionInfo,</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Helvetica\">As I said, this is not a big deal since it can be easily fixed. But the behaviour seems a bit odd.</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Helvetica;min-height:14px\"><br></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Helvetica\">Best regards</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Helvetica\">Rudolf</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Helvetica;min-height:14px\"><br></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Helvetica\">sessionInfo()</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Helvetica\">R version 3.1.0 (2014-04-10)</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Helvetica\">Platform: x86_64-apple-darwin13.1.0 (64-bit)</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Helvetica;min-height:14px\"><br></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Helvetica\">locale:</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Helvetica\">[1] en_US.UTF-8</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Helvetica;min-height:14px\"><br></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Helvetica\">attached base packages:</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Helvetica\"> [1] grid      parallel  stats4    splines   stats     graphics  grDevices utils     datasets  methods   base     </p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Helvetica;min-height:14px\"><br></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Helvetica\">other attached packages:</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Helvetica\"> [1] lme4_1.1-6          Rcpp_0.11.1         Matrix_1.1-3        compareGroups_2.0.2 SNPassoc_1.9-2      DeducerReshape_0.3  Deducer_0.7-7      </p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Helvetica\"> [8] car_2.0-20          e1071_1.6-3         effects_3.0-0       colorspace_1.2-4    foreign_0.8-61      gdata_2.13.3        ggplot2_0.9.3.1    </p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Helvetica\">[15] haplo.stats_1.6.8   Hmisc_3.14-4        Formula_1.1-1       survival_2.37-7     lattice_0.20-29     lawstat_2.4.1       MASS_7.3-32        </p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Helvetica\">[22] mvtnorm_0.9-99991   plyr_1.8.1          scales_0.2.4        TH.data_1.0-3       VGAM_0.9-3          XLConnect_0.2-7     xtable_1.7-3       </p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Helvetica\">[29] JGR_1.7-17          iplots_1.1-7        JavaGD_0.6-1        rJava_0.9-6        </p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Helvetica;min-height:14px\"><br></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Helvetica\">loaded via a namespace (and not attached):</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Helvetica\"> [1] class_7.3-10        cluster_1.15.2      digest_0.6.4        epitools_0.5-7      gtable_0.1.2        gtools_3.4.0        HardyWeinberg_1.5.2</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Helvetica\"> [8] labeling_0.2        latticeExtra_0.6-26 minqa_1.2.3         multcomp_1.3-3      munsell_0.4.2       nlme_3.1-117        nnet_7.3-8         </p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Helvetica\